/// The CANONICAL list is 02 §1.9 and 03 §3.2: text, long_text, number, boolean, select,
/// multi_select, date, composite. The admin UI's vocabulary is deliberately RICHER than this
/// one — "Decimal" and "Measurement" are both `number`, differing only in validation and in
/// whether `attributes.unit` is required. Two more enum values would be two more ALTER TYPE
/// migrations for zero query benefit (03 §3.2).
///
/// `currency` is REFUSED and is not a member. An EAV money value is an amount with no market,
/// no currency FK, no `_minor` suffix and no CHECK — and the first thing anyone does with one
/// is show it to a shopper, which is R02 with a plausible story attached. A price is a
/// `prices` row; a cost is `prices.cost_minor`; a non-price number with a unit is `number`
/// plus `attributes.unit` (03 §3.1).
enum AttributeDataType {
  text
  long_text
  number
  boolean
  select
  multi_select
  date
  composite

  @@map("attribute_data_type")
}

